    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `4ac8a800e`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`171424230`). The author's gate is green on this head: the quick gate against the side branch (184 steps, 0 failed), the `kernel_baseline` pins, the three example catalog suites, and clippy on pathkernel and motion. The light lane and the app clippy ran on the head before the merge of the side branch. The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and has `Refs #4025`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`.\n- The safety floor applies: the region decides where the tool can be. No old planner calls the new code; with the default switch the output is identical.\n- Decision 4 holds a maintainer answer (2026-11-26, \"Yes, to the edge\"): for the material side Outside the tool centre can go to the stock outline.\n- PR #4175 (the law suite) calls `PlanarRegion::new` in two helpers. This PR changes that constructor. The PR that merges second takes a merge of the side branch and fixes the two calls.\n- The `NOT_ORIENTED` guard has no negative test; the body says why.",
