    "body": "New head: `e83a31076`. It is a merge of `origin/side/path-kernel` (`73dc7cb6f`, with #4167 and #4175) into this branch.\n\nClass DELTA: the merge has hand edits. The new head waits for a fresh review. The hand edits are:\n\n1. `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws.rs`: the module list had a conflict. Both sides are kept (`region` from this PR, `registry` and `standins` from the side branch).\n2. `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/kit.rs` `rebuild`: the call to `PlanarRegion::new` now gives `p.plane()` as the first argument.\n3. `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/standins.rs` `pocket_region`: the call now gives `WorkPlane::setup_xy(0.0)?`. The part walls are now `center.loops()`, not `part.loops()`. This is a real finding of the new partition check: the stand-in gave the outline of the pocket as the part walls, but the part walls are the boundary loops of the cutter-centre area. The stand-in geometry changed, not the check. The square pocket and the pocket with an island stay valid regions.\n\nGates on `e83a31076` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`):\n- quick gate against `origin/side/path-kernel`: 185 steps, 0 failed (no ui step);\n- `pathkernel suites: laws`: 72 tests pass (64 law tests and 8 region tests);\n- motion `lib` (`kernel_region`), `kernel_laws` and `pass_start_levels` (`kernel_baseline`): pass;\n- `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: pass;\n- clippy on `camcraft-pathkernel` and `camcraft-motion`: clean.\n",
